+#### ClusterTrustBundle Support
+
+Starting with `v3.8.0`, the Kubernetes Gateway API provider supports [ClusterTrustBundle](https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/geps/gep-5075/) references
+in the `caCertificateRefs` of `BackendTLSPolicy` resources and of the Gateway frontend TLS validation.
+
+This requires the cluster to serve the `certificates.k8s.io/v1` API, available since Kubernetes `v1.37`.
+When the API is not served, or when Traefik is not allowed to watch `ClusterTrustBundle` resources, such references are reported as unsupported kinds.
+
+Therefore, in the corresponding RBACs (see [KubernetesGateway](../reference/dynamic-configuration/kubernetes-gateway-rbac.yml) provider RBACs) the `clustertrustbundles` right has been added.
+
+**Required RBAC Updates:**
+
+```yaml
+  ...
+  - apiGroups:
+      - certificates.k8s.io
+    resources:
+      - clustertrustbundles
+    verbs:
+      - list
+      - watch
+  ...
+```
+
 #### `labelSelector` option deprecation
 
 Starting with `v3.8.0`, the `labelSelector` option of the Kubernetes Gateway API provider is deprecated and will be removed in the next major version.
